The costs and speeds are measured, not estimated from model specs: gpt-5-mini token counts were read from the API's usage on the example (most output tokens are reasoning, so cost follows how much is said, not the video length), and speeds come from a 42 s video and a 2.8 min clip, so the fixed model-loading time could be separated from the per-minute rate. CUDA is left out because no GPU was available to time it, rather than quoting numbers that weren't measured. The CONTRIBUTING.md link waits for #30 so main never links to a missing file. The clone URL is HTTPS so it works without a GitHub SSH key.
